From a0511e4f5f39637ffa56940f08ac3b14899c5411 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] riscv64: build with gcc instead of clang

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [tools/install-static-clang.sh's case statement matches RUNNER_ARCH's "RISCV64" only against lowercase arches, so it falls to the default branch and dies on an unrelated unbound-variable typo before any real clang-vs-gcc decision is made]

ci-before-build.sh's own case statement already excludes riscv64 from
clang on Darwin-only grounds elsewhere, but still routes it through
tools/install-static-clang.sh here. That script's case statement matches
GitHub Actions' RUNNER_ARCH against uppercase tokens for every
architecture it means to support on a native runner (ARM64, ARM, X64,
X86) but, for ppc64le/riscv64/s390x, only against the lowercase
`uname -m` spelling - so on this repo's native riscv64 runners, where
RUNNER_ARCH is "RISCV64", it falls through to the default case and fails
immediately on an unrelated typo (`${CLANG_ARCH}` instead of
`${STATIC_CLANG_ARCH}`) - confirmed from this PR's own first CI run,
before OpenBLAS is even built. Upstream never hits this: their own
riscv64 build runs under QEMU on an arm64 runner, so RUNNER_ARCH there is
"ARM64", which does match.

riscv64 here runs on real native hardware, so it falls back to the gcc
toolchain already in both images instead, the same one every other
riscv64 package in this repo already builds OpenBLAS-dependent Fortran/C
code with - matching 0.3.34.106.0's patch of the same name once upstream
later replaced this script with manylinux-install-clang.
---
 ci-before-build.sh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ci-before-build.sh b/ci-before-build.sh
index 7ad9366..0c29550 100755
--- a/ci-before-build.sh
+++ b/ci-before-build.sh
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ export OPENBLAS_VERSION=$version
 echo "creating wheel from $OPENBLAS_COMMIT (NIGHTLY is $NIGHTLY)"

 case "$PLAT" in
-    loongarch64|ppc64le|s390x|riscv64)
+    loongarch64|ppc64le|s390x)
         ./tools/install-static-clang.sh
         export PATH=/opt/clang/bin:$PATH
         export CC="/opt/clang/bin/clang"
--
2.43.0
